          %p
            where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+space"} standard Borel space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\infty}
            is the one point compactification of the real line. (There is no
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G(\mathbb{R}) \rightarrow \mathbb{R}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \xrightarrow{f} \mathbb{R}
            we first need to embedd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            into
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}_{\infty}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔼
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi id
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}_{\bullet}(id_{\mathbb{R}_{\infty}})
            is defined at each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \in G(\mathbb{R}_{\infty})
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔼
                      %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo ∫
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn ∞
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi dP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{E}_{P}(id_{\mathbb{R}_{\infty}}) =\int id_{\mathbb{R}_{\infty}} \, dP
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔼
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi ω
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ω
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Ω
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi Γ
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi dP
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{E}_{\mu(G(\Gamma(t)(P)))}(f) = \int_{\omega \in \Omega} \Big( \int_{x \in \Omega} f(x) \, d\Gamma_t(\bullet | \omega) \Big) \, dP.
          %p
            Editorial Note: The dictionary formula only makes sense for the configuration space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            being a countable measurable space. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+Borel+space"} standard Borel space
            with cardinality of the continuum and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is a probability measure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(\{i\})=0
            for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in \Omega
            then
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Γ
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma_{i,j}(t)=0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            be a countable measurable set. Note however that
            %a{:href => "#Barandes2025"} Barandes 2025
            (page 5) claims that the stochastic-quantum correspondence extends to uncountable spaces provided the dictionary formula is characterized in terms of probability density functions. He has yet to provide that correspondence and, at present, this nLab author does not understand how that construction can be carried out.
          %h2#interpretations Interpretations
          %p
            Being developed: How
            = succeed "," do
